From 87239db99e5d503da4893e8f10d47524fd7472f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:01:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/63] glm cuda: a decode window's MoE glue fused, EXL3 decode
 tiles at one width, KDA f_b and g_b in one launch

All three keep every value's arithmetic and order, so the bits are the same (decode2_bench, byte for byte):

- tf_glm_topk_group: a window's top-k (tf_glm_topk's own per-row code, now glm_moe::topk_row) and, for the
  EXL3 experts, their compact picks and grouping (tf_exl3_group's own code, now tf_exl3::group_rows in
  exl3_group.cuh) in one block. tf_exl3_down_combine takes the shared expert's row as an extra slot and the
  weights' row stride, and sums in tf_glm_combine's order after the side stream's join. Gone from a decode
  MoE layer: two 2D copies, tf_exl3_group, put_slot and glue.combine. TF_GLM_MOE_FUSE=0 turns it off.
- The common experts run in stages (group, core, combine); run() is unchanged.
- tf_exl3_grouped_1_k6r8 / _k8r8: the grouped kernel at one trellis width (no 15-way switch: 79-80
  registers, not 158), 4 tiles a block and 8 reduction rows, for windows of up to 8 rows on a projection
  the loader verified uniform; tf_exl3_grouped_1_nt4 for 9 to 32 rows where it measured faster.
- glm_mm*_16x2: two linears of one shape in one launch (z: the problem; mm_kernel takes its K slice as an
  argument), for KDA's f_b and g_b in decode windows.

